# Check every text file out with LF, whatever `core.autocrlf` is set to.
#
# The index already stores LF for every text file, so this changes nothing about
# what is committed. It fixes the working tree: on a Windows clone with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the default from Git for Windows) every file arrives as
# CRLF, and then `prettier --check` and `openapi-typescript --check` fail on
# files that are byte-identical to what CI verifies. Shell scripts under
# scripts/ and docker/root/ must also be LF to run at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
*.mkv binary
*.mp4 binary

